Original commit body from cd9788ab7b48e2f610dc972d861195762b8c8a4d:

Six linker families (subprocess, database-query, HTTP-client, GraphQL-client,
GraphQL-resolver, message-queue publish/subscribe) minted synthetic
call_site/function stand-ins whose id {name} slot held a generic linker-category
constant (subprocess_call / db_query / http_client / graphql_client / resolver /
mq_publisher) while Symbol.name carried the specific value -- so a consumer
reconstructing a node's name from its documented stable id got a different
string (collapsing e.g. all subprocess call-sites under one label).

Each factory now routes Symbol.name through the new sanitize_id_name_segment
helper (colons ':' -> '.', ADR-0036 Ruling 1; round-trip documented-lossy, full
fidelity in Symbol.name) into the id name slot. The helper is scoped to these
synthetic stand-ins rather than folded into make_symbol_id globally, because an
always-on chokepoint would also rewrite colon-bearing source identifiers (Obj-C
selectors removeItemAtPath:error:) -- that broader landing is WI-sikar.

Deferred (recorded on WI-vuzaf): websocket (route-vs-URL naming nuance in its
sanitizing wrapper) and gRPC (separate non-canonical grpc: id format).

WI-vuzaf Pattern A. Advances INV-dulah / INV-kurup (G1).

